680	/**
681	 * Fulfil a CARD-funded hosting order from its PAID Stripe session. Safe to expose as a
682	 * server action: it trusts NOTHING from its caller but a Stripe session id, which it
683	 * re-retrieves and re-classifies server-side — a forged or foreign id classifies as
684	 * anything-but-hostOrder and returns a no-op, so no one can place an order billed to
685	 * another account. Called ONLY by lib/fulfil-checkout.ts (the shared webhook+redirect
686	 * bus) AFTER it has credited the card leg to the wallet; this then runs the SAME
687	 * `placeHostingOrderCore` the wallet path uses (same `hostorder:<key>` idempotency),
688	 * so the wallet is debited exactly once and a webhook + redirect can never place two
689	 * accounts. `orderHostingAccountFor`'s own first-month-free atomic claim still decides
690	 * the final price here, exactly as on the wallet path.
